From: openwrt-xiaomi-ax3000t-rd03v2 port
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: request peer RX statistics in the default monitor filter

The monitor PPDU consumer updates station RSSI only with a valid frame
control and AST index. PPDU_END_USER_STATS supplies those fields, but the
default filter omits it; the NSS helper adds it only for Wi-Fi offload.
Consequently host mode delivers payload while station signal stays at zero
and its empty RSSI average is reported as -95 dBm.

Request the peer metadata in the shared default filter. NSS already adds
this bit, so its effective filter is unchanged. This also covers restoring
the default filter after monitor teardown or disabling extended statistics.
Keep the existing RSSI conversion, buffer sizes and low-memory ring counts.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -230,6 +230,7 @@
 const struct htt_rx_ring_tlv_filter ath11k_mac_mon_status_filter_default = {
 	.rx_filter = HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_MPDU_START |
 		     HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_PPDU_END |
+		     HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_PPDU_END_USER_STATS |
 		     HTT_RX_FILTER_TLV_FLAGS_PPDU_END_STATUS_DONE,
 	.pkt_filter_flags0 = HTT_RX_FP_MGMT_FILTER_FLAGS0,
 	.pkt_filter_flags1 = HTT_RX_FP_MGMT_FILTER_FLAGS1,
